  "summary": "Glass beads sewn over carved wood: leopard thrones, elephant masks and spider emblems of Grassfields kings.",
  "description": "Bamileke royal workshops sew imported glass beads — red dominant, then blue and white — over carved wooden armatures to make objects of kingship: leopard-mask kuosi dancers, elephant-mask tappers? — kuosi elephant regalia, beaded spider (afu? — no: spider as fon's wisdom emblem) panels, staffs and enormous royal thrones. Bead color and coverage encode rank; only the fon could commission certain motifs. German colonial disruption, then post-independence revival, kept the ateliers working; today's Grassfields festivals still glow with beaded regalia.",
